Spec: Elevation

Purpose:
  Ascent and descent of a ride from its recorded altitudes, live and at save.

Owns:
  ./elevation.dart
  /test/domain/elevation_test.dart

References:
  /docs/decisions/0002-elevation-from-gps.md
  /lib/tracking/tracking.sdd

Must:
  @ElevationGain has the totals ascent and descent in metres, both never negative.
  Altitudes are smoothed with a trailing running median over the last `5` samples; fewer samples use what exists.
  A change counts only when the smoothed altitude is at least `3` m away from the last counted level; the
    first smoothed sample sets that level and counts nothing.
  Missing (`null`) altitudes are skipped and do not move the level.
  @ElevationAccumulator takes one altitude at a time and exposes the running totals; @ElevationGain.of a list
    gives exactly the totals of feeding that list to an accumulator.
  A list with fewer than two usable altitudes has no elevation: the result is `null`, not `0`.

Must not:
  Read the clock, the database or the platform; units are metres.

Scenario: flat ride with noise
  Given altitudes that wander within `±2` m around one level
  When the gain is computed
  Then ascent and descent are `0`

Scenario: steady climb
  Given altitudes rising from `100` to `200` m in steps of `1` m
  When the gain is computed
  Then the ascent is within `5` m of `100` (the median lags by up to `2` m, the hysteresis holds back
    less than `3` m) and the descent is `0`

Scenario: single spike
  Given a flat ride with one sample `40` m too high
  When the gain is computed
  Then the spike adds nothing

Example:
  altitudes `100`, `110`, `100`: ascent `10`, descent `10`
  altitudes `null`, `null`: `null`
  one altitude: `null`

Tasks:
  [!] #97 Device check: a short ride with a hill on an Android and an iOS device, totals plausible.

Done when:
  `flutter analyze` is clean, `flutter test` passes and `specdd lint` passes.
  A short ride with a hill is recorded on an Android and an iOS device and the totals look plausible.
